          "suggestions": "The agent correctly identified the asset (Transformer 1 at MAIN), the window, and the peak-acetylene sample (2024-01-17, 8 ppm), and the reported gas and current values are consistent with the sensor_stats ranges shown in the trace. It transparently reported that fmsr.interpret_dga failed and fell back to a manual IEC/Rogers ratio and Duval computation, which is a reasonable and honest recovery rather than a fabricated result. The three modes are ranked with confidences, load correlation is assessed using il1/il2/il3/inut, main-tank vs OLTC origin is reasoned via the C2H2/H2 relationship, and an OLTC compartment sample is recommended. Improvements: the visible trace is truncated so the iot.history and interpret_dga calls cannot be directly confirmed; the agent should retry interpret_dga once before falling back, explicitly state the exact hydrogen value from the 2024-01-17 history record rather than an approximate 2800, and optionally call fmsr.get_failure_modes to ground the mode names."
